<% content_for :title, "CLI — Shadwire" %>
<% content_for :description, "Reference for the shadwire CLI: init, add, list, search, info, diff, update, remove and status, with their flags, the JSON output and error handling." %>
<% content_for :head do %>
  <%= tag.style rouge_stylesheet %>
<% end %>

<article class="space-y-12">
  <%= render "docs/header",
        title: "CLI",
        description: "The development tool that copies component source into your app and helps you keep it up to date with the registry." %>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <p class="leading-7">
      After <%= link_to "init", docs_installation_path, class: "font-medium underline underline-offset-4" %>,
      run every command through <%= docs_code("bin/shadwire") %>. The binstub loads the CLI
      from the app's bundle, so everyone on the project uses the same version.
      <%= docs_code("bin/shadwire help COMMAND") %> shows the help for a command.
    </p>

    <%= docs_code_block(@snippets[:quick_reference], language: :shell) %>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <%= docs_h2("Commands") %>

    <%= render "docs/table",
          headers: [ "Command", "What it does" ],
          rows: @commands.map { |command|
            [ docs_code(command[:signature]), command[:summary] ]
          } %>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-8">
    <%= docs_h2("Reference") %>

    <div class="space-y-3">
      <%= docs_h3("status") %>
      <p class="text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
        Describes the project in a single call. Run it first. It is also the only command an
        agent needs to have in its context.
      </p>
      <%= docs_code_block("bin/shadwire status --json", language: :shell) %>
      <%= docs_code_block(@snippets[:status_json], language: :json) %>

      <%= render "docs/table",
            headers: [ "Field", "How to read it" ],
            rows: [
              [ docs_code("installed[].helpers"), "The ui_* methods defined in this app. Calling the helper of a component that is not installed raises NoMethodError." ],
              [ docs_code("installed[].drift"), safe_join([ docs_code("unchanged"), ", ", docs_code("modified"), ", ", docs_code("missing"), " or ", docs_code("unknown"), "." ]) ],
              [ docs_code("stack.importmap"), "Whether importmap and Stimulus are present. The interactive components need both." ],
              [ docs_code("cli.binstub"), safe_join([ "Whether ", docs_code("bin/shadwire"), " exists. If it is false, run ", docs_code("init"), "." ]) ],
              [ docs_code("helpers.includeAllHelpers"), safe_join([ "False means the app turned off Rails' automatic helper inclusion, so each controller needs a ", docs_code("helper"), " call for the ", docs_code("Ui::*Helper"), " modules." ]) ],
              [ docs_code("helpers.legacyHelperPresent"), safe_join([ "An ", docs_code("app/helpers/ui_helper.rb"), " left over from before helpers were split per component. It defines helpers for components you have not installed, and you can delete it." ]) ]
            ] %>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-3">
      <%= docs_h3("search") %>
      <p class="text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
        Search looks at the name, title, description <strong class="font-semibold text-foreground">and</strong>
        the when-to-use text, so you can search for what you need:
        <%= docs_code("form") %>, <%= docs_code("modal") %>, <%= docs_code("overlay") %>,
        <%= docs_code("loading") %>, <%= docs_code("right-click") %>.
      </p>
      <%= docs_code_block(@snippets[:search], language: :shell) %>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-3">
      <%= docs_h3("info") %>
      <p class="text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
        The component's full API. Check it before writing ERB so you are not guessing at
        arguments. It returns <%= docs_code("whenToUse") %>, <%= docs_code("usage") %> snippets,
        <%= docs_code("requiresStimulus") %>, <%= docs_code("registryDependencies") %>, the
        install files, and <%= docs_code("api.components[]") %> with each class's helper,
        variants, sizes, props and attributes.
      </p>
      <%= docs_code_block(@snippets[:info], language: :shell) %>
      <p class="text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
        <%= docs_code("helper") %> is <%= docs_code("null") %> for anything without a
        <%= docs_code("ui_*") %> wrapper: the base superclass, the internal parts a parent
        component renders by itself, and blocks. File contents are left out.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-3">
      <%= docs_h3("add") %>
      <%= docs_code_block(@snippets[:add], language: :shell) %>
      <p class="text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
        Without <%= docs_code("--yes") %>, files that already match the registry are skipped,
        and it asks about the ones you changed. In a non-interactive shell without
        <%= docs_code("--yes") %>, everything is skipped and nothing gets installed.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-3">
      <%= docs_h3("diff") %>
      <p class="text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
        Changes nothing. Marks each file as <%= docs_code("unchanged") %>,
        <%= docs_code("modified") %> or <%= docs_code("missing") %>, with a unified diff for the
        modified ones.
      </p>
      <%= docs_code_block(@snippets[:diff], language: :shell) %>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-3">
      <%= docs_h3("update") %>
      <%= docs_code_block(@snippets[:update], language: :shell) %>
      <%= render layout: "docs/callout", locals: { icon: "triangle-alert", variant: :destructive, title: "update overwrites local edits" } do %>
        Run <code>diff</code> first. <code>update</code> does list what it replaced
        (<code>overwritten</code> and <code>diffs</code> in the JSON output), but only after the
        fact. See <a href="<%= docs_theming_path %>#keeping-your-edits" class="font-medium underline underline-offset-4">how to keep your edits</a>.
      <% end %>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-3">
      <%= docs_h3("remove") %>
      <%= docs_code_block(@snippets[:remove], language: :shell) %>
      <p class="text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
        It only deletes files that belong to the components you remove. The shared base files,
        and any file another installed component still uses, stay in place. Importmap pins that
        nothing uses any more are listed but not removed.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <%= docs_h2("Flags") %>

    <%= render "docs/table",
          headers: [ "Flag", "Commands", "Effect" ],
          rows: @flags.map { |flag| [ docs_code(flag[:flag]), flag[:commands], flag[:description] ] } %>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <%= docs_h2("Errors and exit codes") %>

    <p class="leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
      Exit code 0 means the command worked. If a command could not install a dependency, it
      says so and exits non-zero, so you can rely on the exit code instead of checking the
      Gemfile yourself.
    </p>

    <%= docs_code_block(@snippets[:errors], language: :console) %>

    <p class="leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
      Each error is a single line on stderr that tells you what to do. These are the messages
      for a malformed <%= docs_code("shadwire.json") %>, an unreachable registry, a registry
      that returns HTML, and a missing argument:
    </p>

    <%= docs_code_block(@snippets[:error_messages], language: :text) %>

    <p class="leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
      The exception is <%= docs_code("status") %>, which never fails: it returns
      <%= docs_code('"rails": false') %>, <%= docs_code("registryError") %> or
      <%= docs_code("configError") %> as fields and exits 0. That makes it safe to run
      anywhere, including when an agent loads it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <%= docs_h2("In CI") %>
    <p class="leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
      Every command accepts <%= docs_code("--yes") %> (no prompts), <%= docs_code("--json") %>
      (JSON output) and <%= docs_code("--cwd") %> (run in another directory). This job fails
      the build when an installed component no longer matches the registry:
    </p>

    <%= docs_code_block(@snippets[:ci], language: :yaml) %>

    <p class="leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
      The job needs the <%= docs_code("development") %> group installed; without it,
      <%= docs_code("bin/shadwire") %> will not run.
    </p>
  </section>
</article>
